Comment:
 xemu is a fork of QEMU specialised for emulating the original Microsoft Xbox.
 It therefore carries QEMU's licensing: the project as a whole is distributed
 under the GNU General Public License version 2, with a large number of
 individual files under GPL-2+, LGPL-2.1+, BSD, or MIT terms. Upstream's
 LICENSE file records GPL-2.0 as the license of the combined work.
 .
 This is a summary for the principal components. Upstream additionally
 generates an aggregated third-party license manifest for its binary
 distributions, which this package installs as
 /usr/share/doc/xemu/LICENSE.upstream.txt.

